error[MODE-1]: a local value cannot be stored into global storage: `v` is local to the caller, but `slot` only receives global values
 --> ../../conformance/MODE/MODE-1-mut-storage-list-constructor-bad.hir:5:3
   5 |   slot = [v]
     |   ^^^^^^^^^^ 
 --> ../../conformance/MODE/MODE-1-mut-storage-list-constructor-bad.hir:4:35
   4 | fn put(mut slot: List[String], v: String) -> () {
     |                                   ^^^^^^ provided: `v` is a borrowed parameter; it lives in the caller's region
 --> ../../conformance/MODE/MODE-1-mut-storage-list-constructor-bad.hir:4:18
   4 | fn put(mut slot: List[String], v: String) -> () {
     |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^ required: `slot` is a `mut` parameter; its storage is the caller's and outlives this call
  = help: 1. declare the parameter `take v` (no cost; callers write `take v`, which moves their value into this call)
  = help: 2. `unique v` (deep copy: allocates, costs O(size), and is not allowed under `@noalloc`)
  = note: `copy v` does not help: a copy shares the blocks of `v`, which stay local
